Change: Rename project and binary to `vaultic`, add `VAULTIC_*` env vars

The project formerly known as restic has been renamed to vaultic. The binary
is now called `vaultic` (formerly `restic`), the Go module path changed from
`github.com/restic/restic` to `github.com/vaultic/vaultic`, and the command
sources moved to `cmd/vaultic`.

All vaultic-specific environment variables are now read under the `VAULTIC_`
prefix (for example `VAULTIC_REPOSITORY`, `VAULTIC_PASSWORD`,
`VAULTIC_PASSWORD_FILE`). For backwards compatibility, variables that are not
set fall back to the legacy `RESTIC_` prefixed names, so existing scripts keep
working. When both variants are set, the `VAULTIC_*` variable takes
precedence.

The repository format is unchanged: repositories stay fully compatible with
restic and rustic in both directions. A new interop harness
(`helpers/interop/`, run on demand via the `interop` CI workflow)
continuously verifies cross-client compatibility.

